#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:46
msgid "Customising This Display"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:47
msgid ""
"The title field and the big Post Editing Area are fixed in place, but you "
"can reposition all the other boxes using drag and drop. You can also "
"minimise or expand them by clicking the title bar of each box. Use the "
"Screen Options tab to unhide more boxes (Location, Features, Property "
"Address, Pricing, Linked Contact, Featured Image, Excerpt, Discussion, "
"Comments, Slug, Author, Listing Details, Listing Features, Additional "
"Features, Files and Links) or to choose a 1- or 2-column layout for this "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:52
msgid ""
"Enter a title for your post, for best results enter the full property "
"address. After you enter a title, you’ll see the permalink below, which you "
"can edit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:54
msgid "Post editor"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:54
msgid ""
"Enter the text for your post. There are two modes of editing: Visual and "
"Text. Choose the mode by clicking on the appropriate tab."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:56
msgid ""
"Visual mode gives you a WYSIWYG editor. Click the last icon in the row to "
"get a second row of controls."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:58
msgid ""
"The Text mode allows you to enter HTML along with your post text. Line "
"breaks will be converted to paragraphs automatically."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:60
msgid ""
"You can insert media files by clicking the icons above the post editor and "
"following the directions. You can align or edit images using the inline "
"formatting toolbar available in Visual mode."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:62
msgid ""
"You can enable distraction-free writing mode using the icon to the right. "
"This feature is not available for old browsers or devices with small "
"screens, and requires that the full-height editor be enabled in Screen "
"Options."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:64
msgid ""
"Keyboard users: When you’re working in the visual editor, you can use "
"<code>Alt + F10</code> to access the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:69
msgid "Title and Post Editor"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:75
msgid ""
"You can upload and insert media (images, audio, documents, etc.) by "
"clicking the Add Media button. You can select from the images and files "
"already uploaded to the Media Library, or upload new media to add to your "
"page or post. To manually create an image gallery, select the images to add "
"and click the “Create a new gallery” button."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:77
msgid ""
"You can also embed media from many popular websites including Twitter, "
"YouTube, Flickr and others by pasting the media URL on its own line into "
"the content of your post/page. Please refer to the Codex to learn more "
"about embeds."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:79
msgid "Note on Automatic Gallery Output:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:79
msgid ""
"When your Easy Property Listings gallery settings are set to automatic the "
"images that have been uploaded to this listing will automatically display "
"and you cannot control the image order or exclude images. For full gallery "
"control, disable the automatic gallery output and “Create a new gallery” "
"for each listing."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:84
msgid "Inserting Media"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:92
#. Translators: %s is the location label.
msgid ""
"Add your listing %1$s as this is what powers the search by %2$s in the "
"search widget."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:103
msgid ""
"Add the full listing address and generate the coordinates for the listing. "
"You can drag the pin to adjust the lat/long coordinates of the listing. If "
"you do not check the \"Display Street Address\" option the street number "
"and street will not display to your visitor. You can also hide the map on a "
"per listing basis."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:105
msgid ""
"If you do not check the \"Display Street Address\" option, the street "
"number and street will not display to your visitor."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:107
msgid ""
"Adjust the lat/long coordinates of the listing by dragging the pin to a new "
"location if required. You can also hide the map on a per listing basis."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:112 lib/meta-boxes/meta-box-init.php:814
#: lib/widgets/widget-functions.php:92
msgid "Property Address"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:120
msgid "Search Price/Rent"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:120
msgid ""
"The search price should always be set as this will allow your visitor to "
"narrow down their search. This number will be formatted as per your Easy "
"Property Listings Currency settings."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:122
msgid "Price/Rent Text"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:122
msgid ""
"This allows you to enter text as the price and allows you to enter a range, "
"from price or anything you want to display. When entered this is displayed "
"instead of the Search Price. No formatting is applied to the Price/Rent "
"text so manually format the price you enter e.g. From $600,000."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:124
msgid "Display Price"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:124
msgid ""
"When this is not ticked your \"No Price Label\" will be displayed which you "
"can adjust from settings. Your custom No Price label is currenty:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:126
msgid ""
"Tick this when your listing is pending sale. The price will be replaced "
"with your custom label which is currently:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:128 lib/meta-boxes/meta-box-init.php:1019
msgid "Sale Price"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:128
msgid ""
"Once your listing is sold, you can enter the sale price and you can choose "
"to \"Display Sale Price\" to your visitor."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:133
msgid "Pricing/Rent"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:139
msgid ""
"Search for their name and select the contact and the contact ID will be "
"determined. Publish/Update your listing and their details will be displayed "
"for quick access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help-single.php:144 lib/meta-boxes/meta-box-init.php:1560
msgid "Linked Contact"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:45
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:46
msgid ""
"This screen provides access to all of your posts. You can customize the "
"display of this screen to suit your workflow."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:52
msgid "You can customize the display of this screen’s contents in a number of ways:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:55
msgid ""
"You can hide/display columns based on your needs and decide how many "
"listings to list per screen using the Screen Options tab."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:56
msgid ""
"You can filter the list of listings by post status using the text links "
"above the listings list to only show listings with that status. The default "
"view is to show all listings."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:57
msgid ""
"You can view listings in a simple title list or with an excerpt using the "
"Screen Options tab."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:58
msgid ""
"You can refine the list to show only listings in a specific category or "
"from a specific month by using the dropdown menus above the listings list. "
"Click the Filter button after making your selection. You also can refine "
"the list by clicking on the listings author, category or tag in the "
"listings list."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:64
msgid "Screen Content"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:70
msgid ""
"Hovering over a row in the listings list will display action links that "
"allow you to manage your listings. You can perform the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:72
msgid "Edit"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:72
msgid ""
"takes you to the editing screen for that listing. You can also reach that "
"screen by clicking on the listing title."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:73
msgid "Quick Edit"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:73
msgid ""
"provides inline access to the metadata of your listing, allowing you to "
"update listing details without leaving this screen."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:74
msgid "Trash"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:74
msgid ""
"removes your listing from this list and places it in the trash, from which "
"you can permanently delete it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:75
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:75
msgid ""
"will show you what your draft listing will look like if you publish it. "
"View will take you to your live site to view the listing. Which link is "
"available depends on your listing status."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:81
msgid "Available Actions"
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:88
msgid ""
"You can also edit or move multiple listings to the trash at once. Select "
"the listings you want to act on using the checkboxes, then select the "
"action you want to take from the Bulk Actions menu and click Apply."
msgstr ""

#: lib/includes/admin/help.php:90
msgid ""
"When using Bulk Edit, you can change the metadata (features, author, etc.) "
"for all selected posts at once. To remove a listing from the grouping, just "
"click the x next to its name in the Bulk Edit area that appears."
msgstr ""

